{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "measure_id": "002a",
  "parent_measure_id": "002",
  "title": "Repack compatible Haas CPU decoder matrices",
  "status": "rejected",
  "reason": "The nine-input screen does not show a gain beyond the control drift: Q4_K is 4.61% slower, Q8_0 is 1.02% faster, and the unchanged F16 path is 0.99% slower. Decoder stage medians do not improve consistently. Full-corpus validation is not pursued for this variant.",
  "scope": "screen",
  "conditions": {
    "name": "Haas on Apple Silicon",
    "repository": "https://github.com/uchkw/speech.cpp",
    "tracking_issue": "https://github.com/uchkw/speech.cpp/issues/1",
    "purpose": "Reduce warm latency for one Japanese voice input of a few seconds to 30 seconds while preserving recognition quality.",
    "threads": 4,
    "rounds": 3,
    "decode_on_cpu": true,
    "quality_policy": "exact",
    "latency_count": 9,
    "quality_count": 9,
    "latency_definition": "Time from before sending the first PCM16 chunk through receipt of the terminal result. File reading, model loading and warmup are excluded. Each measured input is warmed once per fresh worker.",
    "aggregation": "Median over rounds for each input, then linearly interpolated p50, p90 and p99 across the measured input medians. RTFx divides total audio duration by summed request time.",
    "literal_cer": "Total Unicode code-point Levenshtein edits divided by total reference code points, including punctuation, symbols and whitespace.",
    "repository_cer": "NFKC followed by removing Unicode punctuation, symbols, separators and whitespace; no case folding or alternate-spelling substitutions. Edits and reference lengths are summed before division.",
    "quality_comparison": "The same quality files on both builds; text and public token/segment text and times are compared exactly. Text from every timestamp-disabled latency round is also compared. A changed CER is not evidence of exact output equality.",
    "latency_timestamps": false,
    "quality_timestamps": true,
    "unobserved_fields": "The worker does not expose raw TDT token IDs, frame indices or duration decisions. These are not claimed to match by this harness.",
    "limitations": [
      "The current corpus is FLEURS Japanese test, with inputs from 6.36 to 28.2 seconds.",
      "The p99 of a small duration-stratified sample is not a precise estimate of production tail latency.",
      "The repository CER is not the published metric accepting alternative spellings of words.",
      "Fresh-process load and first-request times do not reset filesystem or system Metal caches.",
      "This is a nine-input screen, not the full 30-input latency or 650-input quality evaluation. It cannot establish a roughly one-percent improvement.",
      "Decoder stage medians in milliseconds (short/medium/long) are Q4_K 3.041/4.3933/9.4118 to 3.155/4.4425/9.1503; Q8_0 2.463/4.5896/11.7087 to 2.7853/4.3972/8.785; unchanged F16 3.1557/5.1788/10.3904 to 3.1953/5.3148/10.6914. These small timing samples are inconsistent across shapes.",
      "The ordinary decoder copy is lazy. Load-to-ready excludes that first-request copy; first-request time is reported separately.",
      "The candidate uses a different reduction order for selected Q8_0 products. Observed rounding differences and matching public outputs do not prove all possible greedy TDT paths identical.",
      "Memory values are observed peak process footprints across the screen; small differences are not isolated causal memory savings."
    ],
